<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 235 0 R
/E (National Youth Day in India, celebrated on January 12th, honors Swami Vivekananda's ideals to inspire the youth towards a better future. Initiated by the Indian Government in 1984, its objective is to instill national pride and educate youngsters about their rights. The day is marked by various activities, including the National Youth Festival since 1995, promoting cultural exchange and development. In 2024, the festival was held in Nasik, Maharashtra, showcasing the region's rich cultural heritage from January 12th to 16th.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
499 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 235 0 R
/E (The National Youth Festival 2024, held in Nasik, Maharashtra from January 12th to 16th, saw participation from over 18,000 youths representing different states and union territories, including NSS, NYKS, and volunteers. Two studenTS 1\) Joshi Ashray \(CSE 6th Semester\) & 2\) Poorva Ravat \(CSE 6th Semester\) from GTU were selected to represent the institute. Inaugurated by Prime Minister Narendra Modi, along with other dignitaries, the event focused on motivating youth towards Vikshit Bharat 2047 and government schemes. The day concluded with a lively concert by Bollywood singer Niti Mohan, leaving participants with cherished memories and positive energy.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
